course: dictionary
lesson: 10794
title: Vanilla: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Vanilla ice cream» is a flavour: a sweet taste that comes from the seed pods of a climbing orchid plant.
explain: Now look at «plain vanilla». Here vanilla is not a flavour at all. It means plain or ordinary, with nothing special added. The clue is the word «plain» next to it.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If you can swap in "ordinary" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Vanilla is a sweet flavour that comes from the seed pods of a kind of orchid plant.
fact: The vanilla orchid is a climbing plant that grows in warm countries.
fact: Vanilla pods must be dried before they give us the flavour we know.
fact: Informally, «vanilla» means plain or ordinary, with nothing special added.
fact: «Vanilla essence» and «vanilla extract» are flavourings used in baking.
exercise: «The kids' menu had minced-beef patty, chips and vanilla ice cream.» What is vanilla here? | A type of bread | Red | A kind of dog | *A flavour
exercise: «Her new phone is a plain vanilla model.» What does vanilla mean here? | A sweet flavour from an orchid | A bright yellow colour | *Ordinary, with nothing special added | Very expensive
exercise: Vanilla pods grow on a climbing orchid. Where do they grow? | In the desert | Under the sea | *In warm countries | In cold countries
test: Which phrase means ordinary, with nothing special added? | Vanilla ice cream | Vanilla pod | *Plain vanilla | Vanilla extract
test: What must vanilla pods be before they become the flavour? | Painted | *Dried | Frozen | Washed in the sea
exam: Chloe says «plain vanilla» means sweet and creamy. Is she right? | *No, it means plain or ordinary, with nothing special added | No, it means a climbing plant | Yes, it means a sweet flavour from an orchid | Yes, it means a creamy yellow colour
